# jailmgr (jailctl helper)

`jailmgr` provisions and runs multiple IP-bound `jailctl` jails using
one shared read-only base layer (from `base.tar.xz`) and per-jail writable
state (`etc`, `var`, `tmp`, `home`).

New: The script also configures host-side IP aliases automatically
(defaulting to `lo0`) and can optionally generate NPF forwarding rules.

## Workflow

1. Copy the helper script:

   ```sh
   install -m 0755 jailmgr /usr/sbin/jailmgr
   ```

2. Create `/etc/jailmgr.conf` from the sample and customize (including required `JAIL_SUPERVISE_CMD`).

3. Download sets and build the base layer:

   ```sh
   /usr/sbin/jailmgr fetch-sets
   /usr/sbin/jailmgr build-base
   ```

4. Prepare and start all jails (adds aliases on `JAIL_HOST_IF`, default `lo0`):

   ```sh
   /usr/sbin/jailmgr prepare-all
   /usr/sbin/jailmgr start-all
   ```

5. Verify SSH reachability from the host:

   ```sh
   ssh user@10.0.0.1
   ```

## Optional NPF integration

If `NPF_ENABLE=YES`, run:

```sh
/usr/sbin/jailmgr npf-sync
```

This writes `NPF_CONF_SNIPPET` with `rdr` rules based on `NPF_RDR_LIST`.
Include that snippet from `/etc/npf.conf` and optionally set
`NPF_AUTO_RELOAD=YES`.

## Notes

- The host must route `10.0.0.0/24` appropriately (loopback aliases are handled
  automatically by this script).
- `jailctl create -i <ip>` enforces IPv4 bind restriction inside each jail.
- `jailmgr start-jail` uses `jailctl create` followed by `jailctl supervise`.
- By default, `fetch-sets` derives the set URL from `RELEASE` and
  `MACHINE_ARCH` as
  `https://cdn.netbsd.org/pub/NetBSD/NetBSD-${RELEASE}/${MACHINE_ARCH}/binary/sets`.
  You can override it with `NETBSD_MIRROR`.
- Host keys are generated by each jail's `/etc/rc` if missing.
- A sample `rc.d` wrapper can be generated with:

  ```sh
  /usr/sbin/jailmgr gen-rc /etc/rc.d/jailmgr
  echo 'jailmgr=YES' >> /etc/rc.conf
  ```
